# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SCL scenario: raw elevation tiles (~1.5 GB). Reproduce with scenario/fetch_dem.sh
# The derived heightfields under scenario/terrain/ ARE committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
scenario/dem/
scenario/dem_cop/
scenario/dem_cop_hgt/
scenario/dem_srtm_clean/
scenario/terrain/_fine_profile.npy

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SCL scenario: third-party reference photographs. They are properly credited in
# scenario/scl_references.md, but they are CC BY-SA — share-alike conflicts with
# this repo's CC BY 4.0 asset licence, so we cite them instead of shipping them.
# Same rule as the aircraft reference photos. Overlays built on map tiles too.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
scenario/refs/*.jpg
scenario/refs/*.jpeg
scenario/refs/_map_*.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SCL scenery: the terrain .blend is 130 MB of mesh generated in ~6 s from the
# committed heightfields. Rebuild it with
#   blender -b --factory-startup -P scenario/build_scenery.py -- --terrain
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
scenario/scl_terrain.blend

# SCL scenery: render outputs from render_checks.py
scenario/checks/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Portable exports (export/). Regenerate the whole lot with
#   python3 export_frota.py            # ~2 min for the fleet, both LODs
# What IS committed: export/web/*.glb — the light three.js deliverable, about
# 0.5 MB each, so a fresh clone can open export/viewer.html and see the fleet.
# What is NOT: everything below, because it is bulky and regenerable.
#   alta/  ~44 MB per aircraft (GLB + FBX + OBJ + loose textures) = ~400 MB
#   *.usdz  ~3 MB each; AR Quick Look, one command away
# Same rule as scenario/scl_terrain.blend: derived, large, one command to rebuild.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
export/alta/
export/web/*.usdz
export/*/textures_*/
export/.rel_*.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SDSC scenario: raw elevation tiles (~1.4 GB) and their normalised copies.
# Reproduce with scenario_sdsc/fetch_dem.sh
# The derived heightfields under scenario_sdsc/terrain/ ARE committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
scenario_sdsc/dem/
scenario_sdsc/dem_cop/
scenario_sdsc/dem_cop_hgt/
scenario_sdsc/dem_srtm_clean/
scenario_sdsc/terrain/_fine_profile.npy

# The raw Overpass dump (1 MB of JSON). build_osm.py re-downloads it; only the
# converted scenario_sdsc/sdsc_osm.json is committed.
scenario_sdsc/sdsc_osm_raw.json

